<BaseLayout title="The Problem | Arkansas Campaign Data Cooperative" description="Arkansas campaigns cannot organize effectively with incomplete phones, emails, and addresses. Why enhanced data and better tools matter.">
<section class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Problem</p>
        <p class="brand-lockup">Why this cooperative exists</p>
        <h1 transition:name="page-title">Incomplete voter information is an organizing tax.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Campaigns are expected to identify supporters, contact voters, recruit volunteers, raise money, and turn people out—often with outdated phones, missing mobiles, and broken addresses.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/data/">See the L2 data answer</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/platform/">See the Electd platform</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Arkansas campaigns cannot organize effectively with incomplete or outdated voter information.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Many organizations rely heavily on VAN. VAN remains important—but any voter-contact system is only as useful as the data feeding it.</p>
        <h3>Common problems</h3>
        <ul class="problem-list">
          <li>Missing or outdated phone numbers</li>
          <li>Missing mobile numbers for texting</li>
          <li>Incomplete email information</li>
          <li>Old or incorrect mailing addresses</li>
          <li>Duplicate or disconnected voter records</li>
          <li>Valuable contacts stuck in spreadsheets, phones, notebooks, or separate systems</li>
          <li>Local knowledge that never becomes part of a usable campaign database</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>We already work from important Arkansas voter-registration information from the Secretary of State, plus records from voter and ballot-initiative efforts.</p>
          <p class="emphasis">That is a usable foundation on Electd.</p>
          <p class="emphasis-strong">For verified emails, mobiles, and enriched addresses at scale, campaigns need an enhanced file—planned via <a href="/data/">L2</a> and the <a href="/cooperative/">cooperative</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="topic-grid" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
          <a class="topic-card" href="/data/"><h3>L2 Data</h3><p>Enhanced phones, emails, mail, attributes.</p><span class="topic-go">Drill in →</span></a>
          <a class="topic-card" href="/van/"><h3>VAN</h3><p>Strengthen existing tools—don’t abandon them.</p><span class="topic-go">Drill in →</span></a>
          <a class="topic-card" href="/privacy/"><h3>Private contacts</h3><p>Campaign relationships stay firewalled.</p><span class="topic-go">Drill in →</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

</BaseLayout>

